<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The privacy manifest.

  Apple has required one since spring 2024 for any app that uses a
  "required reason" API, and rejects at upload without it. Three declarations
  are asked for and all three are made here.

  ## Tracking: false, and nothing to qualify it

  The app has no advertising identifier, no attribution SDK, no analytics, and
  makes no network request at runtime. `NSPrivacyTrackingDomains` is empty
  because there are no domains at all — not because the ones there are happen
  not to track.

  ## Collected data: none

  Apple's definition of *collection* is transmission off the device. The
  learner's practice history is written to a SQLite file in this app's own
  container by the plugin in `HangyulStorePlugin.swift` and never leaves it, so
  it is not collected under that definition. There is no account for it to
  belong to.

  ## Required-reason APIs: none

  This array was not always empty. It carried
  `NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp` with reason `C617.1`, because
  `@capacitor/filesystem` calls `stat` and reads `modificationTime` — and the
  app reached that code on exactly one path, writing an exported backup into its
  own cache directory before handing it to the share sheet.

  The backup feature was removed, and `@capacitor/filesystem` and
  `@capacitor/share` went with it. `store/app-store/privacy-manifest-audit.md`
  is the per-component audit, and with those two gone it finds no required-reason
  API anywhere in the binary. So the declaration went too: declaring a category
  the app does not use would be as wrong as omitting one it does, and a manifest
  that over-declares is a manifest nobody can check.

  `UserDefaults` is worth naming for the same reason: `@capacitor/preferences`
  was removed from this project precisely so that this file would not have to
  declare `CA92.1`, because the learner's data belongs in the SQLite store and
  a second storage mechanism would have been a second thing to keep in sync.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
